{"name":"Garden Pond","hex":"#afc09e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"},{"term":"pond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inland body of standing water, either natural or man-made, that is smaller than a lake.","An inland body of standing water of any size that is fed by springs rather than by a river."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Chiefly in across the pond: the Atlantic Ocean."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden pond","blocks":[{"text":"A garden pond is a water feature constructed in a water garden or designed landscape, normally for aesthetic purposes, to provide wildlife habitat, or for swimming."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Zahradni_jezirko.jpg/330px-Zahradni_jezirko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_pond","wikidata":"Q2887441"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"},{"title":"Pond","blocks":[{"text":"A pond is a small, still, land-based body of water formed by pooling inside a depression, either naturally or artificially. A pond is smaller than a lake and there are no official criteria distinguishing the two, although defining a pond to be less than 5 hectares in area, less than 5 metres (16 ft) in depth and with less than 30% of its area covered by emergent vegetation helps in distinguishing the ecology of ponds from those of lakes and wetlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg/330px-Cornjum%2C_Martenastate_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pond","wikidata":"Q12719646"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Mute_swan_resting_on_a_garden_pond%2C_22_February_2022.jpg/500px-Mute_swan_resting_on_a_garden_pond%2C_22_February_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Mute_swan_resting_on_a_garden_pond%2C_22_February_2022.jpg/1280px-Mute_swan_resting_on_a_garden_pond%2C_22_February_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Mute_swan_resting_on_a_garden_pond%2C_22_February_2022.jpg/500px-Mute_swan_resting_on_a_garden_pond%2C_22_February_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"On occasion, even large waterbirds may visit garden ponds, such as this mute swan (Cygnus olor).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMute_swan_resting_on_a_garden_pond%2C_22_February_2022.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Waterfall_and_garden.jpg/500px-Waterfall_and_garden.jpg?utm_source=en